{
  "title": "72: Al-Jinn الجن",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقُلْ اُوْحِىَ اِلَىَّ اَنَّهُ اسْتَمَعَ نَفَرٌ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ فَقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا سَمِعْنَا قُرْاٰنًاعَجَبًا ۙ‏(1)\nQUL OOHEYA ELAYYA ANNAHUL ASTAMAA’A NAFARUN MENAL JINNE FA-QAALOO INNAA SAMEA’NAA QURAAANANA’AJABAN.\nSay “It hast been revealed unto me that a party of the jinn hath heard (the Qur’an) and said: “Verily, we have heard a Recital (Qur’an) (which is) Wonderful\nيَّهْدِىْۤ اِلَى الرُّشْدِ فَاٰمَنَّا بِهٖ‌ ؕ وَلَنْ نُّشْرِكَ بِرَبِّنَاۤ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(2)\nYAHDEE ELAL AR-RUSHDE FA AAMANNAA BEHI WA LAN NNUSHREKA BERABBENAA AHADAN.\nGuideth it unto the Right (Way), wherefore believe we in it; and never will we associate anyone with our Lord!\nوَّاَنَّهٗ تَعٰلٰى جَدُّ رَبِّنَا مَا اتَّخَذَ صَاحِبَةً وَّلَا وَلَدًا ۙ‏(3)\nWWAANNAH TAA’AALAA JADDU RABBENAA MAA TAKHAZA SAAHEBATAN WA LAA LAAHO.\nAnd that He, exalted is the Majesty of our Lord! hath taken not a wife nor a son\nوَّ اَنَّهٗ كَانَ يَقُوْلُ سَفِيْهُنَا عَلَى اللّٰهِ شَطَطًا ۙ‏(4)\nWA ANNAHU KAANA YAQOOLO SAFEEHUNAA A’LAL LAAHE SHATATAN.\nAnd that want to speak the foolish ones amongst us, against God, atrocious things\nوَّاَنَّا ظَنَنَّاۤ اَنْ لَّنْ تَقُوْلَ الْاِنْسُ وَالْجِنُّ عَلَى اللّٰهِ كَذِبًا ۙ‏(5)\nWWAANNAA ZANANNAA AN LAN-Y TAQOOLA AL-AENSU WAL JENNU A’LAL LAAHE KAZEBAN.\nAnd that thought we that never utter the humans and jinn any falsehood against God\nوَّاَنَّهٗ كَانَ رِجَالٌ مِّنَ الْاِنْسِ يَعُوْذُوْنَ بِرِجَالٍ مِّنَ الْجِنِّ فَزَادُوْهُمْ رَهَقًا ۙ‏(6)\nWWAANNAH KAANA REJAALUN MENAL AL-AENSE YAU’OOZOONA BEREJAALIN MENAL JINNE FAZAADOOHUM RAHAQAN.\nAnd that individuals from among the humans used to seek protection of the individuals from among the jinn so they increased them (only) in rebellion (against God)\nوَّاَنَّهُمْ ظَنُّوْا كَمَا ظَنَنْتُمْ اَنْ لَّنْ يَّبْعَثَ اللّٰهُ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(7)\nWWAANNAHUM ZANNOOA KAMAA ZANANTUM AN LAN-Y YYABA’ASA LAAHO AHADAN.\nAnd that they (too) thought, as ye think, never would God raise (from the dead) any one!\nوَّاَنَّا لَمَسْنَا السَّمَآءَ فَوَجَدْنٰهَا مُلِئَتْ حَرَسًا شَدِيْدًا وَّشُهُبًا ۙ‏(8)\nWWAANNAA LAMASNAA SAMAAA-AD FAWAJADNAAHAA MULEAT HARASAN SHADEEDAA WWASHUHUBAN.\nAnd that we sought the heavens, but we found it filled with strong guards and flaming darts\nوَّاَنَّا كُنَّا نَقْعُدُ مِنْهَا مَقَاعِدَ لِلسَّمْعِ‌ ؕ فَمَنْ يَّسْتَمِعِ الْاٰنَ يَجِدْ لَهٗ شِهَابًا رَّصَدًا ۙ‏(9)\nWWAANNAA KUNNAA NAQU’UDU MINHAA MAQAAE’EDA LELSSAME’E FAMAN YYASTAMEE’E AL-AAANA YAJID LAHU SHEHAABAN RRASADAN.\nAnd that sat we on some of the seats (there) to (steal) a hearing; but any who would (try now to) listen, findeth a flaming dart in wait for him\nوَّاَنَّا لَا نَدْرِىْۤ اَشَرٌّ اُرِيْدَ بِمَنْ فِى الْاَرْضِ اَمْ اَرَادَ بِهِمْ رَبُّهُمْ رَشَدًا ۙ‏(10)\nWWAANNAA LAA NADREAA AASHARRUN AUREEDA BEMAN FIL ARZE AM ARAADA BEHIM RABBOHUM RASHADAN.\nAnd that we understand not (by this) whether evil be meant for them that are on the earth, or whether willeth their Lord to guide them aright\nوَّاَنَّا مِنَّا الصّٰلِحُوْنَ وَمِنَّا دُوْنَ ذٰلِكَ‌ؕ كُنَّا طَرَآئِقَ قِدَدًا ۙ‏(11)\nWWAANNAA MINNAA AS-SAALEHOONA WA MINNAA DOONA ZAALEK KUNNAA TARAAEQA QEDADAN.\nAnd that some amongst us are good ones, and the others of us are other than that; we are sects following different ways\nوَّاَنَّا ظَنَنَّاۤ اَنْ لَّنْ نُّعْجِزَ اللّٰهَ فِى الْاَرْضِ وَلَنْ نُّعْجِزَهٗ هَرَبًا ۙ‏(12)\nWWAANNAA ZANANNAA AN LAN-Y NNUA’JEZA LAAHA FIL ARZE WA LAN NNUA’JEZAH HARABAN.\nAnd that knew we that never can we defeat (the will of) God in the earth, and never can we defeat Him (in His will) by flight\nوَّاَنَّا لَمَّا سَمِعْنَا الْهُدٰٓى اٰمَنَّا بِهٖ‌ ؕ فَمَنْ يُّؤْمِنْۢ بِرَبِّهٖ فَلَا يَخَافُ بَخْسًا وَّلَا رَهَقًا ۙ‏(13)\nWWAANNAA LAMMAA SAMEA’NAA HODAA AAMANNAA BEHI FAMAN YOAMIM BE-RABBEHI FALAA YAKHAAFO BAKHSAN WA LAA RAHAQAN.\nAnd that, when heard we the guidance, believed we in it; and whosoever believeth in his Lord, he thereafter feareth neither loss nor oppression,\nوَّاَنَّا مِنَّا الْمُسْلِمُوْنَ وَمِنَّا الْقٰسِطُوْنَ‌ؕ فَمَنْ اَسْلَمَ فَاُولٰٓئِكَ تَحَرَّوْا رَشَدًا‏(14)\nWWAANNAA MINNAA AL-MUSLEMOONA WA MINNAA AL-QAASETOONA FAMAN ASLAMA FA-OOLAAA-EKA TAHARRAWA RASHADAN.\nAnd that, of us some are Muslims and of us are the others who are the deviators (from the right path), and whoever submit these pursue the right guidance\nوَاَمَّا الْقٰسِطُوْنَ فَكَانُوْا لِجَهَنَّمَ حَطَبًا ۙ‏(15)\nWA AMMAA AL-QAASETOONA FA KAANOO LE-JAHANNAMA HATABAN.\nAnd as for the deviators, they shall be for the hell, a fuel\nوَّاَنْ لَّوِ اسْتَقَامُوْا عَلَى الطَّرِيْقَةِ لَاَسْقَيْنٰهُمْ مَّآءً غَدَقًا ۙ‏(16)\nWA LLAWE TATANAZZALO A’LAL AT-TAREEQATE LAASQAYNAAHUM MMAAAN GHADAQAN.\nAnd that if they be steadfast on the right way, We would certainly give them water (A sustenance) in abundance\nلِّنَفْتِنَهُمْ فِيْهِ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يُّعْرِضْ عَنْ ذِكْرِ رَبِّهٖ يَسْلُكْهُ عَذَابًا صَعَدًا ۙ‏(17)\nLLENAFTENAHUM FEEHE WA MAN YYUA’REZ A’N ELAA RABBEHI YASLUKHU A’ZAABAN SAA’ADAN.\nThat we may prove them thereby, but whoso turneth away from the remembrance of his Lord, him will He make undergo a severe chastisement\nوَّاَنَّ الْمَسٰجِدَ لِلّٰهِ فَلَا تَدْعُوْا مَعَ اللّٰهِ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(18)\nWA ANNAL AL-MASAAJEDA LILLAAHE FALAA TADU’OOA LAAHA LAAHE AHADAN.\nAnd that, the places for Sajdah (prostration) are for (the remembrance only of) God, so call ye not (therein) any one with God!\nوَّاَنَّهٗ لَمَّا قَامَ عَبْدُ اللّٰهِ يَدْعُوْهُ كَادُوْا يَكُوْنُوْنَ عَلَيْهِ لِبَدًا ؕ‏(19)\nWWAANNAH LAMMAA QAAMA A’ABDU LAAHE YADU’OOHU KAADOO YAKOONOONA A’LAYHE LEBADAN.\nAnd that, when the servant of God (Muhammad) standeth praying unto Him, they surrounded around him, almost stifling\nقُلْ اِنَّمَاۤ اَدْعُوْا رَبِّىْ وَلَاۤ اُشْرِكُ بِهٖۤ اَحَدًا‏(20)\nQUL INNAMAA AADU’OOA RABBEE WA LAA AUSHREKU BEHI AHADAN.\nSay thou (O’ Our Apostle Muhammad!) “I only pray unto my Lord, and I associate not with Him, anyone\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ لَاۤ اَمْلِكُ لَكُمْ ضَرًّا وَّلَا رَشَدًا‏(21)\nQUL INNEE LAA AAMLEKU LAKUM BEKUM WA LAA RASHADAN.\nSay thou “I own not for you any evil or good\nقُلْ اِنِّىْ لَنْ يُّجِيْرَنِىْ مِنَ اللّٰهِ اَحَدٌ  ۙ وَّلَنْ اَجِدَ مِنْ دُوْنِهٖ مُلْتَحَدًا ۙ‏(22)\nQUL INNEE LAN YYUJEERANEAA MENAL LAAHE AHAD WWALAN AAJEDA MIN DOONEHI MULTAHADAN.\nSay: “Never can protect me against God any one, and never find I besides Him, any place of refuge\nاِلَّا بَلٰغًا مِّنَ اللّٰهِ وَرِسٰلٰتِهٖ‌ ؕ وَمَنْ يَّعْصِ اللّٰهَ وَرَسُوْلَهٗ فَاِنَّ لَهٗ نَارَ جَهَنَّمَ خٰلِدِيْنَ فِيْهَاۤ اَبَدًا ؕ‏(23)\nILLAA BALAAGHAN MENAL LAAHE WARESAALAATEH WA MAN YA’ASIL LAAHA WA RASOOLAHU FA-INNAL LAHU NAARA JAHANNAMA KHAALEDEENA FEEHAA ABADAM.\nSave a delivery (of the message) from God, and His messages; and whosoever disobeyeth God and His Apostle, verily, for him shall be the fire of hell, they shall abide in it for ever\nحَتّٰٓى اِذَا رَاَوْا مَا يُوْعَدُوْنَ فَسَيَعْلَمُوْنَ مَنْ اَضْعَفُ نَاصِرًا وَّاَقَلُّ عَدَدًا‏(24)\nHATTAA EZAA RA-AW MAA YOOA’ADOONA FA SA-YA’LAMOONA MAN AAZA’AFU NAASERAN WWAAQALLU A’ADADAN.\nUntil when see they what they are promised, and then shall they know, who is weaker in helpers and fewer in number\nقُلْ اِنْ اَدْرِىْۤ اَقَرِيْبٌ مَّا تُوْعَدُوْنَ اَمْ يَجْعَلُ لَهٗ رَبِّىْۤ اَمَدًا‏(25)\nQUL IN AADREAA AAQAREEBUN MAA TOO-A’DOON AM YAJA’ALU LAHU RABBEE AAMADAN.\nSay: “I know not whether that which ye are promised is nigh or if my Lord hath appointed for it a distant term\nعٰلِمُ الْغَيْبِ فَلَا يُظْهِرُ عَلٰى غَيْبِهٖۤ اَحَدًا ۙ‏(26)\nA’ALEMUL GHAYBE FALAA YUZHERU A’LAA GHAYBEH AHADAN.\n(He alone is) the “Knower of the unseen, and nor doth he reveal his secrets unto any (one else)\nاِلَّا مَنِ ارْتَضٰى مِنْ رَّسُوْلٍ فَاِنَّهٗ يَسْلُكُ مِنْۢ بَيْنِ يَدَيْهِ وَمِنْ خَلْفِهٖ رَصَدًا ۙ‏(27)\nILLAA MANIS ARTAZAA MIN RASOOLIN FA-INNAHU YASLUKU MIN BAYNE YADAYHE WA MIN KHALFEH RASADAN.\nSave unto that one of the Apostles whom He chooseth for verily He causeth a guard to march before him and after him\nلِّيَعْلَمَ اَنْ قَدْ اَبْلَغُوْا رِسٰلٰتِ رَبِّهِمْ وَاَحَاطَ بِمَا لَدَيْهِمْ وَاَحْصٰى كُلَّ شَىْءٍ عَدَدًا‏(28)\nLLEEA’LAMA AN QAD AABLAGHOOA RESAALAATIL RABBEHIM WA AHAATAL BEMAA LADAYHIM WAAHSAA KULLA SHAY-IN A’ADADAN.\nThat He may know that indeed they have delivered the messages of their Lord, and He encompasseth (by His knowledge) all that is with them, and taketh account of everything",
  "merits": "This ‘Makki’ Surah has 28 verses. It is narrated from Imam Ja’far as-Sadiq (a.s.) that frequent recitation of this Surah is a protection from Jinn and the reciter will be in the company of the Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) on the Day of Resurrection. This Surah also protects one from the evil actions of an unjust person.\nPrisoners secure early release by reciting this Surah and those who recite it properly will never face poverty or starvation. Keeping this Surah in one’s possession ensures safety from the Jinn, victory in debate or confrontation, and safety of possession and wealth. Debts are also easily paid back."
